 mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 120%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #000000; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="h3_text" data-groupid="h3" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 120%;"><strong><a style="color: #000000; font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: none;" href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/private-capital/our-insights/global-private-markets-report/private-credit?__hScId__=v710000019ed404b9f799b77b6e96639540&__hRlId__=83d92415980540280000021ef3a0bcd4&__hDId__=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-omcknsl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=edb7a198ac214a9e88d6fa3c994c9e4d&hctky=17208988&hdpid=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-link-id="a845be308db611ec92e885c76187d3bd"><span style="line-height: 120%;"><span style="font-family: Georgia, Times, serif; line-height: 120%;">Private credit enters a more demanding phase﻿</span></span></a></strong></span></h3> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-006: Headline | H3 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --><section id="1008_p1" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p1_text" data-groupid="p1" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>In the news.</strong> Private-credit investors are facing a more challenging environment after several years of unusually strong performance. According to <em>The Wall Street Journal</em>, returns have moderated as interest rate cuts have reduced lending income, and loan defaults have normalized from historically low levels. Some funds have marked down loan values, trimmed dividends, or faced increased redemption pressure from wealthy investors. The sector continues to outperform many public-loan markets, but the period of easy gains appears to be fading. <span style="line-height: 150%;">[</span><a style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: none;" href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019ed404b9f799b77b6e96639540/83d92415980540280000021ef3a0bcd5/83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQF7wXGB2i2hJCvAvq7l-glFwc6j8q26gkt2Qq8GT9PBqEmhZH7DmoRTzuQYbmYwWqRi3Oc3CpL1_egefU_zyYr62s-lU3-xmGsQUuaPA1sO81hQUJ9fzX6MooXs6Df0Ut2Glkzhk1DYep-g4SyQDeJNO3QPPeSecuovDuGUz0nZiUUvNgn6xOc_z0G0ziyuisT1__siP91jhVrzzkKyMjIQUtOgsnlNzZkEO4v_MZgv_TNiW93-jCjtmZ-IYFxJZcjuIABXoUNz73PPh3E54YbUW5WzJbsppcx-fMB2SWfZSvydlMc0XdF3P3dqTjh9KyTPQlmtbpYg3Ai_nqMg3VkSrVSNN1LVOMcxGfe0RVb3k2UTqBQwYa1FGa-jt3plckiMZIotVVLinO3sIEAm8HpdMjA69k0FSsljkQy0ajaaPVMgNy9rOlNu5qxpSVpnsgBy_WZwHzDgjdcOSOEN3ma-CDS_qIZSGmCAG5sHANLBWS2FYZYkmvBUmBJnchazxAaw==" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-link-id="f260e8519d7f11f0b0e1ad3756d0fe1d"><span style="color: #2251ff; text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%;">WSJ</span><span style="line-height: 150%;">] </span></a></span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-001: Divider -->
