<!-- End 1-001: Divider --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-005: Headline | H2 --><section id="1005_h2" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="center" style="padding: 0px 20px 20px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><h2 style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 120%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #000000; font-family: Georgia, Cambria, Times, Times New Roman, serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="h2_text" data-groupid="h2" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 26px; line-height: 120%;">Private credit is becoming less about deploying capital at pace and more about deploying it with precision.</span></h2> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-005: Headline | H2 --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-001: Divider -->
<section id="1001_divider" layout-row="true"> <div layout-row="true"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" layout-row="true" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td align="center" valign="top" class="pad20rl"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="center" valign="top" style="padding: 0px 20px 20px 20px" class="pad20rl"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td style="line-height: 1px !important" align="center" valign="top"><img src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=3f67ada7-a01e-4c02-ab71-8b46fd3106ae" height="1" style="display: block" border="0" alt=""></td> </tr> </tbody></table></td> </tr> </tbody></table></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section>
<!-- End 1-001: Divider --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --><section id="1008_p1" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p1_text" data-groupid="p1" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>On McKinsey.com.</strong> If private credit’s era of easy gains is ending, what comes next? Investors are taking a harder look at credit quality as the sector evolves. Concerns about leveraged credit losses, liquidity, and AI’s potential impact on software companies—which have been among private credit’s biggest borrowers—have led to increased scrutiny of underwriting and due diligence. Yet <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/private-capital/our-insights/global-private-markets-report/private-credit?__hScId__=v710000019ed404b9f799b77b6e96639540&__hRlId__=83d92415980540280000021ef3a0bcd6&__hDId__=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-omcknsl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=450f439f428f4c57939ca4e3b866047d&hctky=17208988&hdpid=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="a6648dc068f511f1a09b53ee6e3ff1ab">the outlook is far from bleak</a></span>, write McKinsey’s Hyder Kazimi, John Spivey, and <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019ed404b9f799b77b6e96639540/83d92415980540280000021ef3a0bcd7/83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6GbIYX-aOjgKue5D2osTH8-WGmG_2R4rHATQa32eEpolDSwc8K4OfB1mi2pk0uDB3GKZzbLdzkjk6pT69V2Rb9DPJvo4XOW4A4PtHPGEBibKcdQo5TOuln5VlCGuC7Ce5vqHyIjIZDDH6WuQB5DzyE0OCq21X-GWSK9s1PBrkivWJVbcI94qOZ0YZbK8NjCASWDWLDOKu4bJIUKNee2qJZYGfudjObivp2dbG56Jy1Misgplj4cCU_fPikfEp4yo-HIhym635iuEq6ElzYmmRGEu-a6ELjHqrioKDavBtCdOtvJz1YIXf_nXgsSxwAGLdA4nceXB7gOTYDASL_PDZtUvVKu6TQKt0796BEsxhmLo_PoVHFAMpSUj9OonsNmX51MrKZNTw5nttNA-BSvIOjCcKjHD5FlfpUsK_lDRl057hb5H9f7cP4X5O5idML7XOwA==" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="3dc24d20699a11f19783a98855ef292c">Warren Teichner</a></span> in the latest chapter of McKinsey’s <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/private-capital/our-insights/global-private-markets-report?__hScId__=v710000019ed404b9f799b77b6e96639540&__hRlId__=83d92415980540280000021ef3a0bcd8&__hDId__=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-omcknsl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=df24b5c3d01a4f42af131bdd7b87de53&hctky=17208988&hdpid=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="b579ca5068f511f1a09b53ee6e3ff1ab"><em>Global Private Markets Report 2026</em></a></span>. Deal volumes were near historic highs in 2025, strategies beyond direct lending are expanding, and fundraising remains resilient.﻿<br><br><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/private-capital/our-insights/global-private-markets-report/private-credit?__hScId__=v710000019ed404b9f799b77b6e96639540&__hRlId__=83d92415980540280000021ef3a0bcd9&__hDId__=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-omcknsl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=2a79e7e189c84d9b90bc821bbac61c07&hctky=17208988&hdpid=83d92415-9805-4028-8f0c-624c24592f0b" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: none;" data-link-id="9f689a609d8111f0ae742962a556baac"><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%;"><span style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); line-height: 150%; text-decoration: underline;">See what’s next for private credit<img src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=cd761513-936e-4a05-8196-6fb668e6a87c" width="20" alt="" data-mce-src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=cd761513-936e-4a05-8196-6fb668e6a87c"></span></span></strong></a></span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --> </td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-001: Divider -->
